('math-compound-angles-01','mathematics','trigonometry','Trigonometric functions','Compound angles','Which identity is correct?','["sin(A+B)=sinA cosB+cosA sinB","sin(A+B)=sinA+sinB","cos(A+B)=cosA cosB+sinA sinB","tan(A+B)=tanA+tanB"]',0,'The sine addition formula is sin(A+B)=sinA cosB+cosA sinB.','foundation',array['jee-main','tg-eapcet','ap-eapcet'],'published','NCERT Mathematics XI; official JEE Main and EAPCET syllabi',now(),'codex-phase3-review','1.0'),
